From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brewie BSP <bsp@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:05:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] posix serial: use immediate byte reads

The POSIX serial backend disabled canonical mode but left VMIN and VTIME
unchanged.  On a native UART those inherited settings can make avrdude wait
for a block or a timer before returning from read(), preventing reliable
STK500v2 synchronization.

Force the same immediate-read behavior used by the AVR protocol diagnostic.

Signed-off-by: Brewie BSP <bsp@example.invalid>
---
 src/ser_posix.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ser_posix.c b/src/ser_posix.c
--- a/src/ser_posix.c
+++ b/src/ser_posix.c
@@ -177,6 +177,9 @@ static int ser_setparams(const union filedescriptor *fd, long baud, unsigned lon
 #endif                          // ECHOKE
 
   termios.c_oflag &= ~(OPOST | ONLCR | OCRNL);
+  termios.c_cc[VMIN] = 1;
+  termios.c_cc[VTIME] = 0;
+
   termios.c_iflag &= ~(INLCR | IGNCR | ICRNL | IGNBRK);
 
 #ifdef IUCLC
-- 
